<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a>–<a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Byelorussian SSR, Soviet Belarus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic was the Soviet republic in the territory of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minsk">Minsk</a>. First proclaimed on 1 January 1919 as the Socialist Soviet Republic of Byelorussia, it was briefly merged with Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanian-byelorussian-soviet-socialist-republic">Litbel</a> and re-established in 1920. A founding member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1922 and of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> in 1945, it declared independence as Belarus in 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/byelorussian-ssr.jpg" alt="Byelorussian Soviet Socialist Republic" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370, reworked by Pianist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Byelorussian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic_(1951%E2%80%931991).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
